    "text": "Last rep of the last set, and Marco's voice drops into that register you've started showing up early for. 'One more.' His hand settles flat and warm on your stomach as you lower — a spotter's hand, he'd say, if anyone asked. 'Breathe. I'll count.' He does. Slow, deliberate, each number landing somewhere low in you. You know what this is: a role, a game you're playing for the man at home who will want every detail tonight. But the counting is real, and so is the heat climbing your throat.",
