    "text": "You stay folded in it, let him hold the count longer than ten, longer than twenty, his hand tracing the long line of your leg while the ache blooms into something warmer. He doesn't rush. He never rushes. 'Good,' he murmurs, 'just like that.' You float on it, half-undone, thinking how you'll describe this stretch to your husband tonight — the exact angle, the exact hand. You haven't given anything away yet. You've just been counted, and held, and you could leave it here, saved.",
