    "text": "You pour yourself something amber and let it warm your throat, moving through the suite in bare feet. The bed is turned down to a crisp white triangle. You catch yourself in the mirror — already flushed, and no one has touched you. You think of your husband picturing all of this, waiting to hear how far you went. The bell sits there, patient as a held breath. You could ring it. Or you could simply finish your drink, keep the ache for later, and carry it home unspent.",
